# ── Build output & generated files — NEVER tracked (ecosystem rule, 2026-10-08) ──
# Only SOURCE is tracked. Everything below is generated by a build, a test run or an
# agent session, and regenerates on demand. Tracking these is what grows a repo
# without bound: paracore/.git reached 493 MB on historical installers alone
# (measured 2026-10-08 — the files were long gone from HEAD, the blobs were not).
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
dist/
build/
installers/
installer_staging/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
target/
.kilo/
.workbuddy-ai/
graphify-out/
*.log

# REPL instruments -- the gates live here (master spec section 4); the rest of
# .repl/ is scratch. Only the allowlisted files below are tracked, so new probe
# files stay local and the repo does not grow.
.repl/*
!.repl/LEARNINGS.md
!.repl/_api_surface_check.py
!.repl/_mcp_engine_drift.py
!.repl/baseline.py
!.repl/check_compliance.py
!.repl/run_section_scope_tests.py
!.repl/verify_gen_docs.py
!.repl/_ext_method_audit.py
!.repl/_ai_tree_check.py

# Build log written by build-addin.ps1 -- generated, not source
scripts/addin_build_log.txt

# VS Code extension build output -- generated, never source
corescript-vscode/out/
corescript-vscode/dist/
